  "overview": {
    "title": "Atlantic sand by town",
    "p1": "El Jadida’s city beach puts Atlantic water within easy reach of the Portuguese walls and the modern town. It is an urban shore — practical, busy in summer, and shaped by trade winds and swell.",
    "p2": "Conditions change with the ocean. Swimming is best when the sea is calm; always respect local flags and advice. For wider resort sand, continue to Sidi Bouzid.",
    "p3": "Use it for a simple swim-and-walk half day between heritage mornings and port evenings."
  },
